{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["The meaning of <b>מיין ושכר.</b> If one vows to be a nazirite and holy, from wine and שכר he abstains according to the translators, who say that שכר is stronger than תירוש, and others said שכר literally: anything from which a person becomes intoxicated." "The meaning of <b>חומץ יין</b> and משרה and the grapes: as a fence, to distance him from wine entirely. And concerning the wife of Manoah, he interpreted 'all impurity, all that comes from the grapevine' [Judges 13:4, 7, 14]." "<b>משרת.</b> It has no parallel form, and the tav is for construct linkage of the feminine noun. Its meaning: anything soaked with grapes. And some say: a cooked beverage."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:31.124491270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}